---
title: One player, retained memory and bounded semantic execution
---
flowchart TD
  accTitle: Player decisions, historical memory and one mission writer
  accDescr: The user sets objectives and can Pause. The lead freezes admission and source, reviews evidence and verifies acceptance. One designated player plans, interprets visible evidence and requests semantic operations through MissionRuntime. Retained campaign memory supports decisions but grants no authority. The writer checks original limits and exact controller and native fences before the real windowed game. Actual frames and operation receipts return to the player and observer. Owned lifecycle and fresh-context continuity are pending acceptance gates; the lead supplies no ordinary gameplay rescue in the deciding mission.
  User["You: objective and boundaries"] --> Lead["Lead: admission and engineering<br/>Review and final verification"]
  Lead -->|"One finite assignment"| Player["Designated player<br/>Plan, interpret, remember, verify"]
  Memory["Evidence-linked campaign memory<br/>Claims, corrections and unfinished Work<br/>Historical, never input authority"] --> Player
  Player -->|"Typed semantic request"| Runtime["One MissionRuntime writer<br/>Original root and child limits"]
  Runtime --> Controller["Controller and native fences<br/>Exact lease, source and deadlines"]
  Controller --> Game["Real windowed CDDA"]
  Game --> Evidence["Visible frames and receipts<br/>Actual effects and uncertainty"]
  Evidence --> Player
  Runtime --> Memory
  Evidence --> Viewer["Observer: objective and progress<br/>Historical context and unknown costs"]
  Runtime --> Viewer
  User -->|"Pause stops new dispatch"| Controller
  Runtime -.-> Gate["Pending acceptance<br/>Owned lifecycle and exact reload<br/>Actual fresh player context"]
